From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 04:21:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Decay and cluster verdict tilts plus BOCPD/cushion sizing
 modifiers, report-only until armed

Rebuilds the decay-allocator-v2 and dd-cushion-bocpd-v6 bundles on this branch (dd builds on da,
and both import decay_verdicts, so they ride the same PR rather than stacking):

- decay_sizing: the Judge's decay verdict and CLUSTER_JUDGE.json as two-sided, heat-conserving
  tilts in pf_allocator; each has its own switch (DECAY_TILT_APPLY.json, CLUSTER_TILT_APPLY.json),
  absent = report-only; applied only when dE[log W] > 0 and the survival envelope passes.
- sizing_modifiers: BOCPD run-length Kelly (IDEA 119) and Grossman-Zhou drawdown cushion
  (IDEA 141), two-sided, billed on missed_growth rails, report-only until armed.
- sizing_modifiers reads each clock's OWN ledger through forward_ledger; a frozen shared legacy
  file is UNMEASURED_SHARED_LEDGER.
- The tilts run before the ceiling guard, so the book still never exceeds the resolved ceiling.

